===Etymology===
A {{borrowing|lv|la|Austria|nocap=1}}, a latinized version of {{etyl|gem|lv}} {{m|goh|ostar||eastern}} (< {{cog|gem-pro|*austraz||eastern}}; [[cf]]. also {{cog|lv|austrumi||east}}), in reference to this land being the {{m|lv|Marchia austriaca||eastern borderland}}. The word was adapted to Latvian spelling ({{suffix|lv||ija}}).

===Pronunciation===
{{audio|lv-riga-Austrija.ogg|lang=lv}}

===Proper noun===
{{lv-proper noun|f|4th}}

# [[Austria]] {{gloss|[[country]] in [[Central Europe]], with [[Viena]] as its [[capital]]}}
